Task: Define scenario schemas

Summary: Implemented complete scenario specification schemas for baseline, intervention, substitution, competition, and network diffusion workflows.

Files Changed:
- src/innovate/scenario/__init__.py (new)
- src/innovate/scenario/schemas.py (new)
- tests/unit/test_scenario_schemas.py (new)

Details:
- ScenarioBase abstract class with validation for common fields
- BaselineScenario: Reference scenario with no interventions
- InterventionScenario: Policy or program interventions with timing and magnitude
- SubstitutionScenario: Technology replacement with incumbent/entrant tracking
- CompetitionScenario: Multi-product markets with market share validation
- NetworkScenario: Network diffusion with topology configuration
- ArtifactEnvelope: Reproducible execution metadata with seed and version
- All scenarios support JSON serialization
- Comprehensive validation with meaningful error messages
- 21 unit tests covering all scenario types and edge cases

Why: This establishes the foundational contract for scenario specifications, enabling deterministic, reproducible experiment workflows across Python and polyglot bindings.
